<title>USA: Cellular stake raised by group.</title>
<headline>Cellular stake raised by group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by HBK Investments L.P. said Tuesday it raised its stake in Cellular Communications International Inc to 676,400 common shares, or 6.4 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said its latest transactions were bought between April 7 and April 25 at prices ranging from $25.50 to $27.25 per share.</p>
<p>Cellular, based in New York, owns and operates cellular telephone systems providing high-quality car and portable telephone services.</p>
</text>
